// REJECTS: Unexpected token
//
// Property aggregation kind is a PARENTHESISED PREFIX -- `(composite) owned: Part[*];` --
// not a modifier attached to the property name. This writes `owned (composite): ...`.
//
// The wrong position is not inert: `name (params): Type[m] { ... }` is the QUALIFIED
// property form, so `owned (composite)` starts down a real grammar path and fails inside
// it. A rewrite that reaches the parenthesis and asks "aggregation kind or parameter
// list?" has a genuine decision to make; one that accepts either reading accepts this file
// and produces a qualified property with a parameter of no type.
###Pure
Class fixture::neg::AggregationAfterName
{
   owned (composite): fixture::neg::Part[*];
}
